<div data-type="problem" id="fs-id1171242609174"><div class="os-problem-container">
<p id="fs-id1171242411358">Find the direction of the induced current in the wire loop shown below as the magnet enters, passes through, and leaves the loop.<span data-type="newline"><br></span>
</p><span data-type="media" id="fs-id1171242160143" data-alt="Figure shows a magnet that is moving into and through the loop with the South pole facing the loop. Position (a) corresponds to magnet approaching the loop; position (b) corresponds to the magnet directly into the loop. Position (c) corresponds to the magnet moving away from the loop.">
