<div data-type="example" id="fs-id1171242446729" class="ui-has-child-title"><header><h3 class="os-title">
  <span class="os-title-label">Example </span>
  <span class="os-number">13.2</span>
  <span class="os-divider"> </span>
</h3></header><section>
<div class="body">
<p id="fs-id1171242239280"></p><h4 data-type="title">A Circular Coil in a Changing Magnetic Field</h4>
A magnetic field <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mstyle mathvariant="bold" mathsize="normal"><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mstyle mathvariant="bold" mathsize="normal"><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mstyle></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> is directed outward perpendicular to the plane of a circular coil of radius <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.50</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.50</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> (<a href="13-2-lenzs-law#CNX_UPhysics_30_02_Circle" class="autogenerated-content" aria-label="View Figure 13.9">Figure 13.9</a>). The field is cylindrically symmetrical with respect to the center of the coil, and its magnitude decays exponentially according to <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1.5</mn><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5.0</mn><msup><mrow><mtext>s</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>−1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1.5</mn><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5.0</mn><msup><mrow><mtext>s</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>−1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> where <em data-effect="italics">B</em> is in teslas and <em data-effect="italics">t</em> is in seconds. (a) Calculate the emf induced in the coil at the times <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5.0</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>s</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5.0</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>s</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> and <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> (b) Determine the current in the coil at these three times if its resistance is <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mn>10</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span>
<div class="os-figure" id="CNX_UPhysics_30_02_Circle"><figure data-id="CNX_UPhysics_30_02_Circle" class="ui-has-child-figcaption">
<span data-type="media" id="fs-id1171242171